      "frightened-adj",
      "afraid-adj"
    ],
    "note": "**Scared** is the everyday word, very common in speech: *I'm scared of the dark.* **Frightened** means much the same and is a little more formal: *The frightened child started to cry.* **Afraid** is used only after a verb (*She was afraid*, not *an afraid girl*), and *I'm afraid* is also a polite way to give bad news: *I'm afraid I can't come.*"
  },
